       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. Doses that high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nIt may be a transposition or a total-daily-dose mix-up. These are some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1700 mg/day total.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** These are common regimens, especially when starting or titrating.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and whether it should be immediate-release or extended-release. I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily as written, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was intentional. I'd recommend checking with pharmacy first."
      }
